SInfo(this,'eth');">eth</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#f3e5f5;color:#6a1b9a" data-s="geo" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'geo');">geo</span></td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#f5f5f5" data-tip="preguntaron" data-lemma="ἐρωτάω" data-morph="V-AAI-3P" data-strongs="G2065">ἠρώτησαν</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#f5f5f5" data-tip="a él" data-lemma="αὐτός" data-morph="P-ASM" data-strongs="G846">αὐτόν</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#ffe0b2" data-tip="¿Tú" data-lemma="σύ" data-morph="P-2NS" data-strongs="G4771">Σὺ</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#ffe0b2" data-tip="quién" data-lemma="τίς" data-morph="I-NSM" data-strongs="G5101">τίς</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#ffe0b2" data-tip="estás siendo" data-lemma="εἰμί" data-morph="V-PAI-2S" data-strongs="G1510">εἶ;</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#ffe0b2" data-tip="Elías" data-lemma="Ἡλίας" data-morph="N-NSM-P" data-strongs="G2243">Ἠλίας</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#ffe0b2" data-tip="estás siendo" data-lemma="εἰμί" data-morph="V-PAI-2S" data-strongs="G1510">εἶ</td><td class="tc-word-cell" style="background:#eee"></td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#f5f5f5" data-tip="está diciendo" data-lemma="λέγω" data-morph="V-PAI-3S" data-strongs="G3004">λέγει</td><td class="tc-word-cell tc-interactive" style="background:#f5f5f5" data-tip="No" data-lemma="οὐ" data-morph="PRT-N" data-strongs="G3756">Οὐκ</td></tr></table></div><div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#555;margin:0.3rem 0;padding:0.3rem 0.5rem;background:#f5f5f5;border-radius:4px"><strong>Lecturas:</strong> <span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#1: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Τί οὖν; Σὺ Ἠλίας εἶ· (𝔓66τίς)</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#2: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Τί οὖν Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#3: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Τί οὖν; Ἠλίας εἶ σύ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#4: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Σὺ οὖν τί; Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#5: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Σὺ τίς εἶ; Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span></div><div style="font-size:0.63rem;color:#999;margin-top:2px;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="font-weight:600">MSS:</span> <span>🔴 Papiros</span> <span>🔵 Unciales</span> <span>⚪ Minúsc.</span> <span>🟣 Versiones</span> <span>🟠 Padres</span> <span>🟢 Byz/Lect</span></div><div class="tc-criteria-expanded"><div class="tc-criterion-item"><strong>Apoyo mayoritario</strong><div class="tc-criterion-exp">La lectura #7.3 tiene el apoyo de la mayoría de manuscritos y diversas tradiciones textuales. Esta amplia atestación sugiere que preserva la forma original.</div></div><div class="tc-criterion-item"><strong>Estructura retórica</strong><div class="tc-criterion-exp">La forma 'Τί οὖν; Ἠλίας εἶ σύ' mantiene el patrón de preguntas directas en el contexto del interrogatorio. Las otras variantes parecen ser reordenamientos estilísticos.</div></div></div><div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#1565c0;margin-top:0.5rem;cursor:pointer" onclick="document.getElementById('exeg-21')?.classList.remove('collapsed');document.getElementById('exeg-21')?.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})">↑ Ver análisis exegético de este versículo</div><div style="margin-top:0.8rem;text-align:center"><a href="tc_deep_dive_John_1_21.html" onclick="if(!this.dataset.ready){this.textContent='⏳ Generando análisis profundo...';this.style.opacity=0.6;return true;}" style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a237e,#0d47a1);color:white;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:600;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(26,35,126,0.3)">🔍 Deep Dive — Análisis completo de esta variante</a><div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#888;margin-top:3px">Si la página no existe, usa el tool <code>critical_apparatus</code> → <code>tc_deep_dive</code> en el MCP server para generarla.</div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb22"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">22</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-22">Εἶπαν οὖν αὐτῷ Τίς εἶ ἵνα ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν τοῖς πέμψασιν ἡμᾶς τί λέγεις περὶ σεαυτοῦ</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-22" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΙΠΑΝ·ΟΥΝ·ΑΥΤΩΙ·ΤΙΣ·ΕΙ·ΙΝΑ·ΑΠΟΚΡΙΣΙΝ·ΔΩΜΕΝ·ΤΟΙΣ·ΠΕΜΨΑΣΙΝ·ΗΜΑΣ·ΤΙ·ΛΕΓΕΙΣ·ΠΕΡΙ·ΣΕΑΥΤΟΥ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=22" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(22)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-22').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-22').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-22')" title="4 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 4 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-22')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-22').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(22)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-22').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-22" class="collapsed spanish-line">Le dijeron: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta a los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div id="vers-22" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Le dijeron: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta a los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Dijéronle: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta á los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>Then said they unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>They said therefore unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?” </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>They said therefore to him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to those who sent us. What sayest thou of thyself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>Then they said to him, Who are you, that we may give an answer to those sending us? What do you say about yourself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>They said then to him, `Who art thou, that we may give an answer to those sending us? what dost thou say concerning thyself?'</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>dixerunt ergo ei quis es ut responsum demus his qui miserunt nos quid dicis de te ipso</div></div><div id="pron-22" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-22" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-22" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.22..." oninput="saveNote(22)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-22')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-22" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-22">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-22" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] Notice they ever ask about his person: he ever refers them to his office.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> περί , concerning ) Each man himself ought) to know himself [ and, if he has any undertaking in particular, he ought to have in readiness a reason [to give] of his undertaking.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> They said therefore ( ειπαν ουν ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_0" class="collapsed comm-body">22. ] Notice they ever ask about his person: he ever refers them to his office . He is no one a voice merely: it is the work of God, the testimony to Christ which is every thing. So the formalist ever in the church asks Who is he? while the witness for Christ only exalts, only cares for Christ&rsquo;s work.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:22] . Ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν , may give an answer ) The people had demanded an answer, and especially the Jewish chief priests. περί , concerning ) Each man himself ought) to know himself [ and, if he has any undertaking in particular, he ought to have in readiness a reason [to give] of his undertaking . V. g.]</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_2" class="collapsed comm-body">They said therefore ( ειπαν ουν ). Second aorist active indicative of defective verb ειπον with α instead of usual ο . Note ουν , inferential here as in verse [John 1:21] though often merely transitional in John. Who art thou? ( Τις ει; ). Same question as at first (verse [John 1:19]), but briefer. That we give answer ( ινα αποκρισιν δωμεν ). Final use of ινα with second aorist active subjunctive of διδωμ with αποκρισιν from αποκρινομα , above, old substantive as in [Luke 2:47]. To those that sent ( τοις πεμψασιν ). Dative case plural of the articular participle first aorist active of πεμπω . What sayest thou of thyself? ( Τ λεγεις περ σεαυτου; ). This time they opened wide the door without giving any hint at all.</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">τίς εἶ / ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> Ellos preguntan sobre su persona, él siempre se refiere a su oficio - es solo una voz, no alguien importante</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Bengel</strong> Cada hombre debe conocerse a sí mismo y tener preparada una razón de su empresa</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Robertson</strong> Esta vez abrieron completamente la puerta sin dar ninguna pista (τί λέγεις περὶ σεαυτοῦ)</div><div class="theme-summary">Alford y Robertson se enfocan en la dinámica de la pregunta, mientras Bengel añade una reflexión sobre el autoconocimiento.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-22')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-22" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística (4 citas) <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-22">▶</span></div><div id="patr-22" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#9e9e9e"><div class="patr-cite-header"><strong>Chrysostom - Homilies on Timothy-Hebrews</strong> <em>(Homily XVI.)</em></div><div class="patr-cite-text">2. Hear then how this blessed person answered to the intention with which they asked
the question, not to the question itself. When they said, “Who art thou?” he did not at once
give them what would have been the direct answer, “I am the voice of one crying in the
wilderness.” But what did he? He removed the suspicion they had formed; for, saith the
Evangelist, being asked, “Who art thou?”</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#9e9e9e"><div class="patr-cite-header"><strong>Gospel of Peter</strong> <em>(Section IV.)</em></div><div class="patr-cite-text">5 John i. 19.
306 John i. 20.
307 John i. 21.
308 John i. 22.
309 John i. 23.
310 John i. 24.
311 Lit. from the side of.
312 John i. 25.
313 John i. 26.
314 Or, in.
315 John i. 2</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#9e9e9e"><div class="patr-cite-header"><strong>John Chrysostom</strong></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Then said they unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself?" Observe them pressing him more vehemently, urging him, repeating their questions, and not desisting; while he first kindly removes false opinions concerning himself, and then sets before them one which is true. For, saith he, "I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the way of the Lord, as said the prophet Esaias." When he had spoken some high and lofty words concerning Christ, as if (replying) to their opinion, he immediately betook himself to the Prophet to draw from thence confirmation of his assertion.</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#9e9e9e"><div class="patr-cite-header"><strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong></div><div class="patr-cite-text">Then he shows how he declared who he was. First, the question of the messengers is given; secondly, his answer (v 23).

They said, Who are you? We must take back an answer to those who sent us. As if to say: We were sent to learn who you are; so tell us, What have you to say about yourself?

Notice John's devotion. He has already fulfilled what the Apostle says, "It is not I who now live, but Christ lives in me" (Gal 2:20). And so he does not answer, "I am the son of Zachary," or this or that, but only the way in which he followed Christ.</div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb23"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">23</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-23">Ἔφη Ἐγὼ φωνὴ βοῶντος ἐν τῇ ἐρήμῳ Εὐθύνατε τὴν ὁδὸν Κυρίου καθὼς εἶπεν Ἠσαΐας ὁ προφήτης</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-23" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΦΗ·ΕΓΩ·ΦΩΝΗ·ΒΟΩΝΤΟΣ·ΕΝ·ΤΗΙ·ΕΡΗΜΩΙ·ΕΥΘΥΝΑΤΕ·ΤΗΝ·ΟΔΟΝ·ΚΥΡΙΟΥ·ΚΑΘΩΣ·ΕΙΠΕΝ·ΗΣΑΙΑΣ·Ο·ΠΡΟΦΗΤΗΣ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=23" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(23)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-23').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-23').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-23').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-23').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-23')" title="13 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 13 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-23')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-23').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-23').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(23)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-23').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-23').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-23" class="collapsed spanish-line">Dijo: Yo soy la voz de uno que clama en el desierto: Enderezad el camino del Señor, como dijo el profeta Isaías.</div><div id="vers-23" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Dijo: Yo soy la voz de uno que clama en el desierto: Enderezad el camino del Señor, como dijo el profeta Isaías.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Dijo: Yo soy la voz del que clama en el desierto: Enderezad el camino del Señor, como dijo Isaías profeta.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>He said, I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the way of the Lord, as said the prophet Esaias.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>He said, I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the way of the Lord, as said Isaiah the prophet. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>John replied in the words of Isaiah the prophet:  “I am a voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way for the Lord.’”  </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>He said, I [am] [the] voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the path of [the] Lord, as said Esaias the prophet. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He said, "I am a voice crying in the wilderness:" "Make straight" "the way of the Lord," as Isaiah the prophet said. Isa. 40:3 </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>He said, `I <FI>am<Fi> a voice of one crying in the wilderness: Make straight the way of the Lord, as said Isaiah the prophet.'</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>ait ego vox clamantis in deserto dirigite viam Domini sicut dixit Esaias propheta</div></div><div id="xrefs-23" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 40:3" data-es="Voz que clama en el desierto: Barred camino á Jehová: enderezad calzada en la soledad á nuestro Dios." data-gr="ק֣וֹל קוֹרֵ֔א בַּ/מִּדְבָּ֕ר פַּנּ֖וּ דֶּ֣רֶךְ יְהוָ֑ה יַשְּׁרוּ֙ בָּ/עֲרָבָ֔ה מְסִלָּ֖ה לֵ/אלֹהֵֽי/נוּ" data-lxx="φωνὴ βοῶντος ἐν τῇ ἐρήμῳ ἑτοιμάσατε τὴν ὁδὸν κυρίου εὐθείας ποιεῖτε τὰς τρίβους τοῦ θεοῦ ἡμῶν" title="Voz que clama en el desierto: Barred camino á Jehová: enderezad calzada en la so…">Isaiah 40:3</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 40:5" data-es="Y manifestaráse la gloria de Jehová, y toda carne juntamente la verá; que la boca de Jehová habló." data-gr="וְ/נִגְלָ֖ה כְּב֣וֹד יְהוָ֑ה וְ/רָא֤וּ כָל בָּשָׂר֙ יַחְדָּ֔ו כִּ֛י פִּ֥י יְהוָ֖ה דִּבֵּֽר" data-lxx="καὶ ὀφθήσεται ἡ δόξα κυρίου καὶ ὄψεται πᾶσα σὰρξ τὸ σωτήριον τοῦ θεοῦ ὅτι κύριος ἐλάλησεν" title="Y manifestaráse la gloria de Jehová, y toda carne juntamente la verá; que la boc…">Isaiah 40:5</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:28" data-es="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy enviado delante de él." data-gr="αὐτοὶ ὑμεῖς ⸀μοι μαρτυρεῖτε ὅτι ⸀εἶπον· Οὐκ εἰμὶ ἐγὼ ὁ χριστός, ἀλλ’ ὅτι Ἀπεσταλμένος εἰμὶ ἔμπροσθεν ἐκείνου." data-lxx="" title="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy env…">John 3:28</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 1:16" data-es="Y á muchos de los hijos de Israel convertirá al Señor Dios de ellos." data-gr="καὶ πολλοὺς τῶν υἱῶν Ἰσραὴλ ἐπιστρέψει ἐπὶ κύριον τὸν θεὸν αὐτῶν·" data-lxx="" title="Y á muchos de los hijos de Israel convertirá al Señor Dios de ellos.">Luke 1:16</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 1:17" data-es="Porque él irá delante de él con el espíritu y virtud de Elías, para convertir los corazones de los padres á los hijos, y los rebeldes á la prudencia de los justos, para aparejar al Señor un pueblo apercibido." data-gr="καὶ αὐτὸς προελεύσεται ἐνώπιον αὐτοῦ ἐν πνεύματι καὶ δυνάμει Ἠλίου, ἐπιστρέψαι καρδίας πατέρων ἐπὶ τέκνα καὶ ἀπειθεῖς ἐν φρονήσει δικαίων, ἑτοιμάσαι κυρίῳ λαὸν κατεσκευασμένον." data-lxx="" title="Porque él irá delante de él con el espíritu y virtud de Elías, para convertir lo…">Luke 1:17</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 1:76" data-es="Y tú, niño, profeta del Altísimo serás llamado; Porque irás ante la faz del Señor, para aparejar sus caminos;" data-gr="καὶ σὺ ⸀δέ, παιδίον, προφήτης Ὑψίστου κληθήσῃ, προπορεύσῃ γὰρ ⸀ἐνώπιον κυρίου ἑτοιμάσαι ὁδοὺς αὐτοῦ," data-lxx="" title="Y tú, niño, profeta del Altísimo serás llamado; Porque irás ante la faz del Seño…">Luke 1:76</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 1:79" data-es="Para dar luz á los que habitan en tinieblas y en sombra de muerte; Para encaminar nuestros pies por camino de paz." data-gr="ἐπιφᾶναι τοῖς ἐν σκότει καὶ σκιᾷ θανάτου καθημένοις, τοῦ κατευθῦναι τοὺς πόδας ἡμῶν εἰς ὁδὸν εἰρήνης." data-lxx="" title="Para dar luz á los que habitan en tinieblas y en sombra de muerte; Para encamina…">Luke 1:79</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 3:4" data-es="Como está escrito en el libro de las palabras del profeta Isaías que dice: Voz del que clama en el desierto: Aparejad el camino del Señor, Haced derechas sus sendas." data-gr="ὡς γέγραπται ἐν βίβλῳ λόγων Ἠσαΐου τοῦ ⸀προφήτου· Φωνὴ βοῶντος ἐν τῇ ἐρήμῳ· Ἑτοιμάσατε τὴν ὁδὸν κυρίου, εὐθείας ποιεῖτε τὰς τρίβους αὐτοῦ." data-lxx="" title="Como está escrito en el libro de las palabras del profeta Isaías que dice: Voz d…">Luke 3:4</span></div><div id="pron-23" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-23" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-23" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.23..." oninput="saveNote(23)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-23')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-23" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-23">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-23" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> εὐθύνατε is used as compendiously expressing ἑτοιμάσατε … εὐθείας ποιεῖτε.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> Ἐγὼ φωνή , I the Voice ) An abbreviated mode of expression; I am that person, of whom it has been said; the Voice of one crying.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> Common imperfect active (or second aorist active) of φημ , to say, old defective verb.<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv23_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv23_0" class="collapsed comm-body">23. ] These words, which by the other Evangelists are spoken of John as the fulfilment of the prophecy, appear from this place to have been first so used by himself . They introduce the great closing section of the prophecy of Isaiah (ch. 40 66) so full of the rich promises and revelations of the Messiah and His kingdom. εὐθύνατε is used as compendiously expressing ἑτοιμάσατε … εὐθείας ποιεῖτε . By implication, the Baptist, quoting this opening prophecy of himself, announces the approaching fulfilment of the whole section.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv23_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv23_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:23] . Ἐγὼ φωνή , I the Voice ) An abbreviated mode of expression; I am that person, of whom it has been said; the Voice of one crying . John was also himself crying. εὐθύνατε ) ἑτοιμάσατε εὐθείας ποιεῖτε , [Luke 3:4] , notes. ἡσαΐας ὁ προφήτης , Isaiah the prophet ) Formerly, saith he, there were prophets : now the kingdom of God is nearer at hand.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv23_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv23_2" class="collapsed comm-body">He said ( εφη ). Common imperfect active (or second aorist active) of φημ , to say, old defective verb. I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness ( Εγω φωνη βοωντος εν τη ερημω ). For his answer John quotes [Isaiah 40:3]. The Synoptics ([Mark 1:3]; [Matthew 3:3]; [Luke 3:4]) quote this language from Isaiah as descriptive of John, but do not say that he also applied it to himself. There is no reason to think that he did not do so. John also refers to Isaiah as the author of the words and also of the message, " Make straight the way of the Lord " ( Ευθυνατε την οδον του κυριου ). By this language ( ευθυνω in N.T. only here and [James 3:4], first aorist active imperative here) John identifies himself to the committee as the forerunner of the Messiah. The early writers note the differences between the use of Λογος (Word) for the Messiah and φωνη (Voice) for John.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-23')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-23" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 3 temas · 13 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-23">▶</span></div><div id="patr-23" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptd9b432ad').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan el Bautista como precursor y heraldo de Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptd9b432ad" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (c.354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.19]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John the Baptist, in proportion as he was greater than those born of women, and was more humble in his acknowledgment of the Lord, obtained the grace of being the friend of the Bridegroom; zealous for the Bridegroom, not for himself; not seeking his own honor, but that of his Judge, whom as a herald he preceded"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (c.540-604) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John declares himself to be the voice, i. e. because he precedes the Word, and, through his ministry, the Word of the Father is heard by man"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (c.1225-1274) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"God the Father sent the precursor John, who came to be in time, in order to make known his Word, which was conceived from eternity. And so he fittingly says, I am a voice"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los padres concuerdan unánimemente en que Juan el Bautista fue enviado como precursor y heraldo de Cristo. Su función era preparar el camino y dar testimonio del Verbo divino.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptf9de2e68').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan como 'la voz' y Cristo como 'el Verbo'</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptf9de2e68" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (c.540-604) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Ye know that the only-begotten Son is called the Word of the Father. Now we know, in the case of our own utterance, the voice first sounds, and then the word is heard. Thus John declares himself to be the voice, i. e. because he precedes the Word, and, through his ministry, the Word of the Father is heard by man"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Origen of Alexandria</strong> (c.185-254) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, exégeta, discípulo de Clemente de Alejandría (Alejandría/Cesarea)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Or%C3%ADgenes" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But he cries and shouts that both those who are far off may hear him speaking and those who have departed from God and those who have lost keenness of their hearing may understand the greatness of what is said, since it is proclaimed with a loud voice"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los padres desarrollan la metáfora de Juan como 'voz' que precede y anuncia al 'Verbo' (Cristo). La voz prepara para escuchar la Palabra divina.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptf1277f2d').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>El desierto como símbolo espiritual</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptf1277f2d" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (c.540-604) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John crieth in the wilderness, because it is to forsaken and destitute Judaea that he bears the consolatory tidings of a Redeemer"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Origen of Alexandria</strong> (c.185-254) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, exégeta, discípulo de Clemente de Alejandría (Alejandría/Cesarea)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Or%C3%ADgenes" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.23]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Now the necessity of the voice of one crying in the wilderness is that the soul—which is devoid of God and destitute of truth (for what other wilderness is there than this?)"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los padres interpretan el desierto tanto literal como espiritualmente, representando el estado del alma alejada de Dios que necesita preparación para recibir a Cristo.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb24"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">24</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-24">Καὶ ἀπεσταλμένοι ἦσαν ἐκ τῶν Φαρισαίων</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-24" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΚΑΙ·ΑΠΕΣΤΑΛΜΕΝΟΙ·ΗΣΑΝ·ΕΚ·ΤΩΝ·ΦΑΡΙΣΑΙΩΝ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=24" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(24)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-24').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-24').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-24').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-24').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-24')" title="9 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 9 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-24')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-24').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(24)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-24').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-24').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-24" class="collapsed spanish-line">Y los que habían sido enviados eran de los fariseos.</div><div id="vers-24" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Y los que habían sido enviados eran de los fariseos.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Y los que habían sido enviados eran de los Fariseos.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>And they which were sent were of the Pharisees.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>And they had been sent from the Pharisees. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>Then the Pharisees who had been sent </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>And they were sent from among the Pharisees. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>And those who had been sent were of the Pharisees. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>And those sent were of the Pharisees,</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>et qui missi fuerant erant ex Pharisaeis</div></div><div id="pron-24" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-24" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-24" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.24..." oninput="saveNote(24)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-24')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-24" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-24">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-24" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> Luthardt thinks that it imports, there were some ἀπεσταλμένοι present, who belonged to the sect of the Pharisees ( ἦσαν δὲ καὶ ἐκ τῶν Φαρ.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> Ἐκ τῶν φαρισαίων , of the Pharisees ) who made a great point of Jewish baptism; and acknowledged the baptism of John to be a thing of great moment, not to be administered except by one having a Divine…<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> They had been sent ( απεσταλμενο ησαν ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv24_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv24_0" class="collapsed comm-body">24. ] The reason of this explanation being added is not very clear. Lücke, with whom De Wette agrees, refers it to the apparent hostility of the next enquiry: but I confess I cannot see that it is more hostile than the preceding. Luthardt thinks that it imports, there were some ἀπεσταλμένοι present, who belonged to the sect of the Pharisees ( ἦσαν δὲ καὶ ἐκ τῶν Φαρ . ἀπεσταλμένοι ), which the words will hardly bear: see below. Might it not be to throw light on their question about baptizing , as the Pharisees were the most precise about all ceremonies, lustrations, &c.? Origen makes this a new deputation: but he is plainly wrong: see the οὖν below. Euthymius gives another reason yet: ἐπεσημήνατο καὶ τὴν αἵρεσιν αὐτῶν , ἐμφαίνων τὸ περίεργον τούτων καὶ σκολιόν . Abandoning the οἱ (see var. readd.), we must render, And they (i.e. the whole deputation) were (or had been ) sent by the Pharisees; which will make it more probable that the explanation refers to the nature of the following question. ἀποστέλλομαι … ἐκ has occurred above, [John 1:19] , which gives additional probability to the reading of the text.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv24_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv24_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:24] . Ἐκ τῶν φαρισαίων , of the Pharisees ) who made a great point of Jewish baptism; and acknowledged the baptism of John to be a thing of great moment, not to be administered except by one having a Divine mission. The evangelist is wont to set down certain, as it were, parentheses, as to causes, as to place, as to occasions, as to ends, as to effects, as to hindrances, of things, actions and speeches, and similar decisions, by means of which the subjects, which are in hand, may the more clearly be understood, [John 1:28] ; [John 1:45] ; [John 3:24] ; [John 4:8] ; [John 6:4] ; [John 7:5] ; [John 7:39] ; [John 8:20] ; [John 8:27] ; [John 9:14] ; [John 9:22] ; [John 10:22-23] ; [John 11:13] ; [John 11:30] ; [John 12:33] .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv24_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv24_2" class="collapsed comm-body">They had been sent ( απεσταλμενο ησαν ). Periphrastic past perfect passive of αποστελλω . From the Pharisees ( εκ των Φαρισαιων ). As the source ( εκ ) of the committee of Sadducees (verse [John 1:19]).</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">ἐκ τῶν Φαρισαίων</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> La razón de esta explicación no es clara, posiblemente para explicar su pregunta sobre el bautismo ya que los fariseos eran precisos sobre ceremonias</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Bengel</strong> Los fariseos daban gran importancia al bautismo judío y reconocían que el bautismo de Juan requería misión divina</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Robertson</strong> Fueron enviados desde (ἐκ) los fariseos como fuente del comité de saduceos</div><div class="theme-summary">Hay acuerdo en que los fariseos tenían interés especial en el bautismo, pero difieren en si eran parte del comité o una fuente separada.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-24')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-24" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 2 temas · 9 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-24">▶</span></div><div id="patr-24" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptcdd37a66').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Autoridad para bautizar</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptcdd37a66" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (s.IV-V (354-430)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.24]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And they which were sent were of the Pharisees, that is, of the chief men among the Jews; and they asked him and said unto him, Why baptizest thou then, if thou be not the Christ, nor Elias, nor a prophet? As if it seemed to them audacity to baptize, as if they meant to inquire, in what character baptizest thou?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (s.XIII (1225-1274)) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.25]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Their questions concerned his office of baptizing. Hence he says that they asked him, Why then do you baptize? Here we should note that they are asking not to learn, but to obstruct. For since they saw many people coming to John because of the new rite of baptism, foreign both to the rite of the Pharisees and of the law, they became envious of John and tried all they could to hinder his baptism."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que los fariseos cuestionaban la autoridad de Juan para bautizar, viendo su bautismo como una novedad que requería justificación divina.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt7db7e274').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Motivaciones de los fariseos</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt7db7e274" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#f44336"><div class="patr-cite-header">❌ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (s.VI (540-604)) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.24]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But still those who were sent inquire further: Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the prophet? Because this was said not from a desire to learn the truth, but from the malice of pursuing rivalry, the Evangelist silently made known when he added, saying: And those who had been sent were from the Pharisees. As if he openly said: Those men inquire of John about his actions who do not know how to seek teaching, but only how to envy."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#f44336"><div class="patr-cite-header">❌ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (s.IV (349-407)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.25]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"What folly, what insolence, what ill-timed officiousness! Ye were sent to learn who and whence he might be, not to lay down laws for him also. This too was the conduct of men who would compel him to confess himself to be the Christ."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres están de acuerdo en que los fariseos no preguntaban por sincero deseo de aprender, sino por envidia y malicia hacia Juan.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb25"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">25</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-25">καὶ ἠρώτησαν αὐτὸν καὶ εἶπαν αὐτῷ Τί οὖν βαπτίζεις εἰ σὺ οὐκ εἶ ὁ Χριστὸς οὐδὲ Ἠλίας οὐδὲ ὁ προφήτης</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-25" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΚΑΙ·ΗΡΩΤΗΣΑΝ·ΑΥΤΟΝ·ΚΑΙ·ΕΙΠΑΝ·ΑΥΤΩΙ·ΤΙ·ΟΥΝ·ΒΑΠΤΙΖΕΙΣ·ΕΙ·ΣΥ·ΟΥΚ·ΕΙ·Ο·ΧΡΙΣΤΟΣ·ΟΥΔΕ·ΗΛΙΑΣ·ΟΥΔΕ·Ο·ΠΡΟΦΗΤΗΣ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=25" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(25)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-25').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-25').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-25').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-25').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-25')" title="13 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 13 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-25')" title="2 comentarios exegéticos">📚 2 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-25').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-25').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="1 referencias cruzadas">🔗 1 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(25)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-25').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-25').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-25" class="collapsed spanish-line">Y le preguntaron, y le dijeron: ¿Por qué, pues, bautizas, si tú no eres el Cristo, ni Elías, ni el profeta?</div><div id="vers-25" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Y le preguntaron, y le dijeron: ¿Por qué, pues, bautizas, si tú no eres el Cristo, ni Elías, ni el profeta?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Y preguntáronle, y dijéronle: ¿Por qué pues bautizas, si tú no eres el Cristo, ni Elías, ni el profeta?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>And they asked him, and said unto him, Why baptizest thou then, if thou be not that Christ, nor Elias, neither that prophet?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>And they asked him, and said unto him, Why then baptizest thou, if thou art not the Christ, neither Elijah, neither the prophet? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>asked him, “Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?” </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>And they asked him and said to him, Why baptisest thou then, if thou art not the Christ, nor Elias, nor the prophet? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>And they asked him and said to him, Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>and they questioned him and said to him, `Why, then, dost thou baptize, if thou art not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the prophet?'</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>et interrogaverunt eum et dixerunt ei quid ergo baptizas si tu non es Christus neque Helias neque propheta</div></div><div id="xrefs-25" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Deuteronomy 18:18" data-es="Profeta les suscitaré de en medio de sus hermanos, como tú; y pondré mis palabras en su boca, y él les hablará todo lo que yo le mandare." data-gr="נָבִ֨יא אָקִ֥ים לָ/הֶ֛ם מִ/קֶּ֥רֶב אֲחֵי/הֶ֖ם כָּמ֑וֹ/ךָ וְ/נָתַתִּ֤י דְבָרַ/י֙ בְּ/פִ֔י/ו וְ/דִבֶּ֣ר אֲלֵי/הֶ֔ם אֵ֖ת כָּל אֲשֶׁ֥ר אֲצַוֶּֽ/נּוּ" data-lxx="προφήτην ἀναστήσω αὐτοῖς ἐκ τῶν ἀδελφῶν αὐτῶν ὥσπερ σὲ καὶ δώσω τὸ ῥῆμά μου ἐν τῷ στόματι αὐτοῦ καὶ λαλήσει αὐτοῖς καθότι ἂν ἐντείλωμαι αὐτῷ" title="Profeta les suscitaré de en medio de sus hermanos, como tú; y pondré mis palabra…">Deuteronomy 18:18</span></div><div id="pron-25" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-25" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-25" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.25..." oninput="saveNote(25)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-25')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-25" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-25">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-25" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] On οὐδὲ … οὐδέ , see note on [John 1:13].<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> Why then baptizest thou? ( Τ ουν βαπτιζεισ; ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv25_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv25_0" class="collapsed comm-body">25. ] On οὐδὲ … οὐδέ , see note on [John 1:13] . This question shews probably that they did not interpret Isa 40:3 of any herald of the Messiah. They regarded baptism as a significant token of the approach of the Messianic Kingdom, and they asked, &lsquo;Why baptizest thou, if thou art no forerunner of the Messiah?&rsquo;</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv25_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv25_1" class="collapsed comm-body">Why then baptizest thou? ( Τ ουν βαπτιζεισ; ). In view of his repeated denials (three here mentioned). If thou art not ( ε συ ουκ ε ). Condition of first class. They did not interpret his claim to be "the voice" to be important enough to justify the ordinance of baptism. Abrahams (Studies in Pharisaism and the Gospels) shows that proselyte baptism was probably practised before John's time, but its use by John was treating the Jews as if they were themselves Gentiles.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-25')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-25" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 2 temas · 13 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-25">▶</span></div><div id="patr-25" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt45cc66b1').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Autoridad para bautizar</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt45cc66b1" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (s.IV-V (354-430)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.24]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And they which were sent were of the Pharisees, that is, of the chief men among the Jews; and they asked him and said unto him, Why baptizest thou then, if thou be not the Christ, nor Elias, nor a prophet? As if it seemed to them audacity to baptize, as if they meant to inquire, in what character baptizest thou?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (s.XIII (1225-1274)) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.25]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Their questions concerned his office of baptizing. Hence he says that they asked him, Why then do you baptize? Here we should note that they are asking not to learn, but to obstruct. For since they saw many people coming to John because of the new rite of baptism, foreign both to the rite of the Pharisees and of the law, they became envious of John and tried all they could to hinder his baptism."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que los fariseos cuestionaban la autoridad de Juan para bautizar, viendo su bautismo como una novedad que requería justificación divina.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptaa9c08bd').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Motivaciones de los fariseos</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptaa9c08bd" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#f44336"><div class="patr-cite-header">❌ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (s.VI (540-604)) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.24]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But still those who were sent inquire further: Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the prophet? Because this was said not from a desire to learn the truth, but from the malice of pursuing rivalry, the Evangelist silently made known when he added, saying: And those who had been sent were from the Pharisees. As if he openly said: Those men inquire of John about his actions who do not know how to seek teaching, but only how to envy."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#f44336"><div class="patr-cite-header">❌ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (s.IV (349-407)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.25]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"What folly, what insolence, what ill-timed officiousness! Ye were sent to learn who and whence he might be, not to lay down laws for him also. This too was the conduct of men who would compel him to confess himself to be the Christ."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres están de acuerdo en que los fariseos no preguntaban por sincero deseo de aprender, sino por envidia y malicia hacia Juan.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb26"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">26</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-26">Ἀπεκρίθη αὐτοῖς ὁ Ἰωάννης λέγων Ἐγὼ βαπτίζω ἐν ὕδατι μέσος ὑμῶν ἕστηκεν ὃν ὑμεῖς οὐκ οἴδατε</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-26" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΑΠΕΚΡΙΘΗ·ΑΥΤΟΙΣ·Ο·ΙΩΑΝΝΗΣ·ΛΕΓΩΝ·ΕΓΩ·ΒΑΠΤΙΖΩ·ΕΝ·ΥΔΑΤΙ·ΜΕΣΟΣ·ΥΜΩΝ·ΕΣΤΗΚΕΝ·ΟΝ·ΥΜΕΙΣ·ΟΥΚ·ΟΙΔΑΤΕ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=26" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(26)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-26').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-26').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-26').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-26').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-26')" title="20 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 20 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-26')" title="2 comentarios exegéticos">📚 2 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-26').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(26)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-26').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-26').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-26" class="collapsed spanish-line">Juan les respondió diciendo: Yo bautizo con agua; mas en medio de vosotros está uno a quien vosotros no conocéis.</div><div id="vers-26" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Juan les respondió diciendo: Yo bautizo con agua; mas en medio de vosotros está uno a quien vosotros no conocéis.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Y Juan les respondió, diciendo: Yo bautizo con agua; mas en medio de vosotros ha estado á quien vosotros no conocéis.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>John answered them, saying, I baptize with water: but there standeth one among you, whom ye know not;</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>John answered them, saying, I baptize in water: in the midst of you standeth one whom ye know not, </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>“I baptize with water,” John replied, “but among you stands One you do not know. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>John answered them saying, I baptise with water. In the midst of you stands, whom ye do not know, </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>John answered them, saying, I baptize in water, but One stands in your midst whom you do not know; </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>John answered them, saying, `I baptize with water, but in midst of you he hath stood whom ye have not known, this one it is who is coming after me, who hath been before me,</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>respondit eis Iohannes dicens ego baptizo in aqua medius autem vestrum stetit quem vos non scitis</div></div><div id="pron-26" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-26" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-26" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.26..." oninput="saveNote(26)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-26')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-26" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-26">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-26" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> οὐκ οἴδατε , ye know not ) He addresses the inhabitants of Jerusalem, who had not been present at the baptism of Jesus: and he whets their desires, that they may be anxious to become acquainted with H…<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> In the midst of you standeth ( μεσος υμων στηκε ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv26_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv26_0" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:26] . Μέσος [30] ) ὑμῶν , in the midst of you ) especially at the time of His baptism. ἕστηκεν ) Hath taken His stand [statuit sese]. οὐκ οἴδατε , ye know not ) He addresses the inhabitants of Jerusalem, who had not been present at the baptism of Jesus: and he whets their desires, that they may be anxious to become acquainted with Him. [30] δέ , but ) The Antithesis is to be taken from the pre-eminence of Him who followed after John: He truly baptizes with the Holy Ghost, ver. 33. V. g.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv26_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv26_1" class="collapsed comm-body">In the midst of you standeth ( μεσος υμων στηκε ). Adjective as in [John 19:18], not εν μεσω υμων . Present active indicative of late verb στηκω from perfect stem εστηκα . John had already baptized Jesus and recognized him as the Messiah. Whom ye know not ( ον υμεις ουκ οιδατε ). This was the tragedy of the situation ([John 1:11]). Apparently this startling declaration excited no further inquiry from the committee.</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">μέσος ὑμῶν ἕστηκεν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Bengel</strong> En medio de vosotros especialmente en el tiempo de su bautismo, se ha establecido (ἕστηκεν) - estimula sus deseos</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Robertson</strong> μέσος como adjetivo, no ἐν μέσῳ ὑμῶν - Juan ya había bautizado a Jesús y lo reconoció como Mesías</div><div class="theme-summary">Bengel se enfoca en el aspecto temporal del bautismo, mientras Robertson hace una distinción gramatical sobre μέσος y el contexto cronológico.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-26')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-26" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 3 temas · 20 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-26">▶</span></div><div id="patr-26" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt02009ffa').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Naturaleza del bautismo de Juan vs Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt02009ffa" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (s.VI (540-604)) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John baptizeth not with the Spirit, but with water; not being able to remit sins, he washes the bodies of the baptized with water, but not their souls with pardon. Why then doth he baptize, when he doth not remit sins by baptism? To maintain his character of forerunner."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (s.XIII (1225-1274)) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"You should not be disturbed, if I, who am not the Messiah, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet, baptize; because my baptism is not completive but imperfect. For the perfection of baptism requires the washing of the body and of the soul; and the body, by its nature, is indeed washed by water, but the soul is washed by the Spirit alone."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (s.V (376-444)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For I, he says, am bringing in an introductory Baptism, washing those defiled by sin with water for a beginning of penitence and teaching them to go up from the lower unto the more perfect."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Hay consenso unánime en que el bautismo de Juan era preparatorio e imperfecto, lavando solo el cuerpo con agua, mientras que Cristo bautiza con el Espíritu Santo.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt6a01a718').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Presencia oculta de Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt6a01a718" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (s.IV-V (354-430)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"I baptize with water; but there standeth One among you whom ye know not. For, very truly, He was not seen, being humble, and therefore was the lamp lighted."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (s.IV (349-407)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But there standeth One among you, whom ye know not. Reasonable it was that Christ should mingle among the people as one of the many, because everywhere He taught men not to be puffed up and boastful."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (s.V (376-444)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Much enduringly does the blessed Baptist bear with the fault finders: and very seasonably does he make the declaration regarding himself a basis of saving preaching: and teaches those who were sent from the Pharisees now even against their will that Christ was within the doors."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que Cristo estaba presente pero oculto entre la gente debido a su humildad, siendo desconocido por los fariseos.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt5dd5e0bc').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan como precursor y testigo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt5dd5e0bc" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (s.IV-V (354-430)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.27]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And yet, just notice how this forerunner of his Lord, of one who is God and man, how much he humbles himself. No one has arisen greater among those born of women than this man, and here he is, questioned about whether he is himself the Christ."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory the Dialogist</strong> (s.VI (540-604)) <span class="patr-meta">— Papa, reformador, Doctor de la Iglesia (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_I" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.26]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Why then doth he baptize, when he doth not remit sins by baptism? To maintain his character of forerunner. As his birth preceded our Lord's birth, so his baptism preceded our Lord's baptism."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres reconocen unánimemente el papel único de Juan como precursor que prepara el camino para Cristo a través de su testimonio y bautismo.</div></div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('tc-26')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tc-26" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">⚖️</span> Crítica Textual <span style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#ff9800">(3 lecturas)</span> <span class="arrow" id="arrow-tc-26">▶</span></div><div id="tc-26" class="collapsed section-content tc-section"><div class="tc-verdict" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem"><div class="tc-verdict-text"><strong>Veredicto:</strong> La lectura #8.1 (ἕστηκεν) es probablemente original, con amplio apoyo manuscrito incluyendo P66, A, C, Δ, Θ, Ψ y la mayoría de manuscritos. La lectura #8.2 (εἱστήκει) representa un cambio al pluscuamperfecto para mayor precisión temporal. La lectura #8.3 (στήκει) es una forma contracta que simplifica la morfología verbal. Todas las variantes expresan esencialmente la misma idea de 'estar de pie' pero con diferentes matices temporales.</div><div class="consensus-bar" style="max-width:200px"><div style="width:90%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#4caf50;font-weight:600;margin-left:4px">Confianza: alta</span><div class="tc-impact"><strong>Impacto:</strong> Las diferencias en las formas verbales afectan sutilmente el aspecto temporal de la acción, pero no cambian el significado fundamental de que alguien está presente entre ellos. El tiempo presente enfatiza la realidad inmediata de la presencia del Mesías.</div></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><table class="tc-tabl